Ask the adapter's storage-buffer limit for, rather than settling for the default.

create_webgpu_context raises five limits from what the adapter reports — buffer size, storage
binding size, workgroup storage, invocations, workgroup dimensions — and omits this one, so a
device is created with the specification's floor of eight storage buffers per compute stage
however many the adapter would have allowed. The frame pipeline's combine kernel binds nine.

Sent nowhere yet; it belongs upstream on Halide PR #8955, which this tree is a checkout of.
diff --git a/src/runtime/webgpu.cpp b/src/runtime/webgpu.cpp
